verses.text:
To which of the angels, then, did God ever say,
“My Son you are;
this day I have fathered you”?{d}
Or again,
“I myself will be Father to him,
and he for his part will be Son to me”?{e}

Of the angels he says,
“He makes his angels winds,
and his ministers a flame of fire.”{g}

But of the Son he says,
“Your throne, O God, is forever and ever,
and the scepter of uprightness is the scepter of his kingdom.{h}

You have loved justice and hated lawlessness;
therefore God, your God, has anointed you
with the oil of gladness beyond your companions.”

And,
“In the beginning, Lord, you laid the foundation of the earth,
and the heavens are the work of your hands.{i}

To which of the angels has he at any time said,
“Take your seat at my right hand
while I lay your foes beneath your feet as a footstool”?{k}

Someone has testified somewhere,
“What is man, that you remember him,
or the son of man, that you care for him?{b}

when he says,
“I will make your name known to my brothers;
among the gathered congregation I will sing hymns to you.”{g}

And again,
“I will put my trust in him.”{h}
And again,
“Here I am, and the children God has given me.”{i}

That is why I was angry with that generation,
and I said, ‘Their hearts always go astray;
they have not known my ways.’

God fixes another day, a “today,” speaking through David a long time later in the words already cited,
“Today, if you should hear his voice,
do not make your hearts hard.”{d}

So also Christ did not glorify himself by becoming a high priest; it was given him by the one who said to him,
“You are my Son;
today I have become your Father.”{b}

As he also says in another place,
“You are a priest forever,
in the order of Melchizedek.”{c}

It will not be like the covenant that I made with their ancestors
on the day when I took them by the hand
to lead them out of the land of Egypt;
because they did not continue in my covenant,
I too disregarded them, says the Lord.{d}

That is why, as he comes into the world, Christ says,
“Sacrifice and offering you did not want,
but a body you have made ready for me;{b}

For,
“In just a little while,
the one who is coming will come and will not delay;{m}

but my righteous one will live by faith,
and if he shrinks back,
my soul takes no delight in him.”{n}

And you have forgotten the word of encouragement which speaks to you as to sons:
“My son, do not treat lightly the discipline of the Lord,
nor give up when he rebukes you;{d}

So we may boldly say,
“The Lord is my help; I will have no fear.
What can mortals do to me?”{d}
